{"id": "613a45db-c7ae-492b-9774-276f2eb20411", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T11:54:17.946845", "source": "user", "parent_id": "0ce98434-d606-45eb-a4b1-a15dd2e7404d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is an initial-inspection turn for a design-only task on whether the MDGEN model accurately recovers fast timestep dynamics (e.g., oscillations in torsion angles) that are missing in subsampled molecular dynamics trajectories. Please do the following and report back — do NOT draft the full experiment design yet, do NOT run experiments, and do NOT fabricate results or reference numbers you cannot cite from provided sources. Concretely, I need: (1) **Repository inspection**: list what is present under /workspace (files, READMEs, configs, scripts, datasets, any MDGEN-related code or papers already provided). For each item, give a one-line description and indicate whether it is clearly relevant to the research question. If something is absent, say so explicitly — absence is informative. (2) **Topic/status check on a few setup details** that the brief leaves open: (a) the target MDGEN variant/checkpoint and its training-time stride or subsampling factor, (b) the choice of system(s) for evaluation (e.g., alanine dipeptide, a small peptide, fast-folding proteins — explicitly enumerate which, if any, are mentioned in provided material), (c) the ground-truth data source for fast dynamics (e.g., high-frame-rate all-atom MD, e.g.g., an external repository), (d) compute/runtime assumptions, and (e) the 'fast dynamics' proxy metric(s) under consideration (e.g., reweighted torsional autocorrelation times, spectral density of φ/ψ, Karplus-type J-coupling reconstructed from reweighted frames, free-energy along Ramachandran). For each, say whether the supplied documents fix the choice, suggest it, or leave it open and free for us to propose. (3) **Proposed approach**: a short, source-grounded design sketch — what comparisons would directly answer the question, what controls are needed (e.g., ground-truth high-frame MD vs. subsampled MD vs. MDGEN-augmented trajectories; linear interpolation or spline interpolation baselines; negative controls such as time-reversed or shuffled frames), and what feasibility risks you foresee. (4) **Consequential assumptions and uncertainties**: a brief list of assumptions you intend to make, and the uncertainties / unknowns (from the brief's unknowns list) that most need clarification. End with an explicit decision request: propose a check-in point after we align on approach before you produce the final experiment design document. Cite only items visible in provided material; do not invent study facts, datasets, latency targets, or relative ordering of models.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the MDGEN model accurately recover the fast timestep dynamics (e.g., oscillations in torsion angles) that are missing in subsampled molecular dynamics trajectories?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
