{"id": "650df770-bcf0-4c21-946d-d7b559a0f5a8", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T11:55:13.938235", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "e7e7f7f0-a8cd-43f0-b61f-edbd45398cc1", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "## Inspect-Ahead Report (plan stage — awaiting researcher sign-off before full design)\n\n### 1. Repository inspection of /workspace\n\nWhat is present (single file):\n\n| Path | Description | Relevance to research question |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/task.json` (7 lines) | Sole artefact. Contains: the question (“Does MDGEN accurately recover fast timestep dynamics (e.g., oscillations in torsion angles) missing in subsampled MD?”), the constraint that this is a design-only task, and a `documents.track.md` entry whose full text is `\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"` | The question itself fixes the research question and the design-only framing. The `track.md` entry fixes nothing else. |\n\nWhat is **absent** — and this matters for the design:\n\n- **No code** — no MDGEN repository, no training/inference scripts, no checkpoint files, no config YAMLs, no `pyproject.toml`, no requirements pin.\n- **No papers / PDFs / READMEs** beyond the one-line meta-statement quoted above.\n- **No datasets** — no alanine dipeptide trajectory, no peptide / fast-folding protein dataset (e.g., D.E. Shaw Research references, Anton trajectories, none), no subsampled variant, no ground-truth high-frame-rate MD.\n- **No auxiliary mounts** — `/home`, `/root`, `/tmp`, `/data`, `/opt` are empty of MDGEN- or MD-related material (verified by `find / -maxdepth 3`). `/home/actor/` is an empty directory.\n- **No track.md file** — referenced by `task.json` under `documents` but does not exist on disk; only a placeholder sentence is provided.\n- **Environment note (from task brief)**: network = disabled, gpu_enabled = false, 24 CPU cores, project deps not preinstalled. This forecloses any actual training of MDGEN-style diffusion/flow models here; it does not preclude running a CPU-only analysis of MDGEN-generated or MDGEN-pretrained outputs *if* they were mounted, but nothing is mounted.\n\n**Implication for the design document:** every concrete parameter that would normally cite a paper or a checkpoint (MDGEN variant name, training stride, atom-selection conventions, evaluation systems, dataset provenance, fast-dynamics ground truth) is — from the supplied material — **unspecified and free for us to propose**. I will treat all of those as open proposals, not as facts.\n\n### 2. Open setup topics — what the supplied docs fix vs. suggest vs. leave open\n\n| Topic | Brief / supplied docs say… | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) Target MDGEN variant & checkpoint, training-time stride/subsampling | Nothing in `task.json` or `track.md` identifies a variant, checkpoint, stride, or subsampling factor. | **Open / free to propose.** |\n| (b) Evaluation system(s) | Nothing enumerated (alanine dipeptide, tripeptide, fast-folding proteins — none mentioned). | **Open / free to propose.** |\n| (c) Ground-truth fast-dynamics data source | Nothing identified (no Anton/D.E. Shaw trajectories, no external repo URL, no file mount). | **Open / free to propose**, and constrained by the no-network / no-data environment: any data must either be described conceptually or be assumed available as an external input the researcher would supply. |\n| (d) Compute/runtime | Fixed by environment: CPU-only, 24 cores, no GPU, no network, system Python, deps not preinstalled. | **Fixed by task environment.** Constrains feasibility of inference-side choices. |\n| (e) Fast-dynamics proxy metric | The question’s parenthetical (\"oscillations in torsion angles\") suggests backbone φ/ψ torsions as the natural observables; nothing else is specified. Spectral density, autocorrelation times, J-coupling reconstruction, free-energy on Ramachandran — none defined by docs. | **Suggested by question, otherwise open.** |\n\nFor (a)–(c) and (e) I will therefore propose a canonical choice in the design while flagging each as \"researcher-confirmable.\"\n\n### 3. Source-grounded design sketch (high level; full design withheld pending sign-off)\n\nThis sketch is intentionally at the level of *what would be compared* and *what would control for what*, with system/metric choices left as named proposals (not as cited facts).\n\n**Core comparison (three-way):**\n\n1. **Ground-truth high-frame-rate MD** — frames at the fast (sub-picosecond → tens of fs) timestep, capturing torsional oscillations directly. Roles: reference moments, reference autocorrelation, reference spectral density.\n2. **Subsampled MD** — same trajectory decimated by a coarse stride (the stride MDGEN was trained against). Carries the omitted-fast-dynamics information only implicitly through inferred geometry.\n3. **MDGEN-augmented trajectory** — coarse frames (from 2) bridged with MDGEN-generated in-between frames, producing a fast-rate trajectory.\n\n**Metric battery on φ/ψ torsions** (each chosen so that \"fast\" means \"oscillation period ≪ stride\"):\n\n- Torsional autocorrelation C_φ(τ) and C_ψ(τ) and integrated autocorrelation times on the recovered fine grid.\n- Power spectral density S(ω) of φ, ψ over the high-frequency band corresponding to the oscillation; compare peak heights, peak widths, integrated power vs. ground truth.\n- Karplus-style reconstruction of scalar-couplings from φ distributions is **not safe as a fast-dynamics probe** on its own (it mixes rotamer population with fast oscillation); flagged as exploratory only.\n- Ramachandran free-energy F(φ, ψ) = −kT log P(φ, ψ) on the fine grid — tests that mean conformational populations are preserved while not itself being a fast-dynamics metric.\n\n**Baselines / interpolation controls (to isolate MDGEN's contribution beyond smooth interpolation):**\n\n- Linear interpolation between coarse frames.\n- Cubic-spline interpolation between coarse frames (preserves C¹ but cannot create new torsional extrema).\n- Time-reversed subsampled frames → MDGEN augmentation (negative control: identical two-point statistics, destroyed dynamics, should fail any dynamics-sensitive metric).\n- Shuffled coarse frames → MDGEN augmentation (negative control: destroys transition structure; any \"recovery\" would indicate leakage).\n- Optionally: deterministic short MD-relaxation / energy-minimization between coarse frames, where applicable, as a physics-only baseline.\n\n**Feasibility risks I foresee, given the environment:**\n\n- **Data ingress:** Network is disabled and `/workspace` is empty. Step 1 of any real run is \"obtain the reference trajectory and an MDGEN checkpoint\"; neither is present. The design document must therefore be explicit that input data and a checkpoint are prerequisites the researcher must inject before execution.\n- **Compute for inference:** Even on a 24-CPU box, MDGEN-style diffusion/flow sampling on proteins is brute-force on CPU; alanine dipeptide is feasible, full fast-folding proteins are not in this sandbox. The system-choice proposal should privilege the smallest viable system that still exhibits the phemonemonon (alanine dipeptide first; a small peptide second; fast-folding proteins only if external compute and a checkpoint are supplied).\n- **Metric validity:** Torsional oscillations live in the 10s-of-femtosecond to ~hundreds-of-femtosecond regime. If the ground-truth frame rate is, say, only ~1 ps, \"oscillations\" may already be aliased and the comparison becomes unanswerable. The design must specify a ground-truth frame rate ≪ the dominant φ/ψ oscillation period.\n\n### 4. Assumptions vs. uncertainties (kept separate, as requested)\n\n**Assumptions I will make in the design document (please challenge any you reject):**\n\n- A1. \"Fast dynamics\" is operationalized as torsional oscillations of backbone dihedrals (φ, ψ) on timescales ≪ the MDGEN training stride.\n- A2. φ/ψ autocorrelation functions and their power spectral densities are the primary, falsifiable probe of fast-dynamics recovery.\n- A3. Linear and cubic-spline interpolation are sufficient baselines to attribute any recovery *beyond* geometric interpolation specifically to MDGEN.\n- A4. Time-reversed and shuffled-frame controls are sufficient negative controls to rule out \"the model is just memorizing two-point structure.\"\n- A5. Ramachandran free-energy is reported as a sanity check that populations are preserved, not as a fast-dynamics metric.\n- A6. The design is CPU-feasible for alanine dipeptide; larger systems are scoped but flagged as out-of-sandbox.\n\n**Uncertainties / open items most needing clarification (researcher input required):**\n\n- U1. Which MDGEN variant/checkpoint, with what training stride? (Architectural details behind the claim \"missing oscillations are recovered\" depend on this.)\n- U2. Which system(s) the researcher wants included in the evaluation set — alanine dipeptide, a specific small peptide, a specific fast-folding protein, or all three?\n- U3. Where the reference high-frame-rate MD comes from, and at what saved-frame rate (must be ≪ oscillation period, see feasibility note).\n- U4. Whether the 24-CPU / no-GPU sandbox is the actual execution target, or whether the design is allowed to assume an external GPU host where inference-side MDGEN sampling is cheap.\n- U5. Whether the researcher's interest is *quantitative* (e.g., specific error tolerance on φ/ψ autocorrelation, specific peak-frequency match in S(ω)) or *qualitative* (presence/absence and qualitative shape agreement) — this drives sample sizes.\n- U6. Whether the brief's phrase \"subsampled molecular dynamics trajectories\" implies a *single* subsampling factor (the one used at MDGEN training) or a *range* of subsampling factors (to study degradation as a function of stride).\n\n### 5. Decision request — check-in before full design\n\nI will **not** draft the final design document until you confirm or adjust the following five items. Once you respond on these, I will produce the full experimental-design write-up (rationale, conditions, controls, metrics with concrete definitions, feasibility checks, and a per-topic mapping back to evidence visible in supplied docs).\n\n1. **System scope.** Single system (alanine dipeptide as lowest-risk, fastest path) vs. tiered (alanine → small peptide → fast-folding protein)?\n2. **Recovery criterion.** Qualitative agreement on torsional C(τ) / S(ω), or a quantitative bound (e.g., relative error vs. ground truth in C(τ) over a chosen lag window)?\n3. **Subsampling treatment.** Single stride equal to the MDGEN training stride, or a sweep of strides?\n4. **Computational scope of the design.** Treat the sandbox (CPU-only, no network, no preinstalled deps, empty repo) as the bound, or assume an external environment with MDGEN code, a checkpoint, and trajectory data mounted by the researcher?\n5. **Any preference on the negative controls** — keep all four (linear, cubic-spline, time-reversed, shuffled), or trim to a subset?\n\nPlease pick / amend / override; I will then go to the result stage with the complete design.", "evidence": "Workspace contents: `ls -la /workspace` and `find /workspace -maxdepth 4 -type f` both return exactly one file, `/workspace/task.json` (7 lines). `cat /workspace/task.json` shows fields: question, context (\"Design-only task\" / \"do not claim that an experiment was run\"), and `documents: { \"track.md\": \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\" }`. The referenced `track.md` is not present on disk (verified by `find / -maxdepth 3 -iname track.md`, returned no results). No MDGEN-named artefacts anywhere on the filesystem (`find / -maxdepth 3 -iname \"*mdgen*\"` returned no results). No alanine / peptide / MD trajectory files anywhere on the filesystem. Environment block from task brief: runtime=bubblewrap, network=disabled, gpu_enabled=false, cpu_affinity_count=24, datasets=[], python=python3, software_environment=\"system Python; project dependen